---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="PROVE — Hypothesis-to-MVP Framework — Pratyush Shrivastav"
  description="An operating model for rapidly validating product hypotheses through aggressively scoped one-week MVPs. Disciplined execution at speed."
>
  <section class="work-hero">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <div class="work-breadcrumb reveal">
        <a href="/">← Back to home</a>
      </div>

      <div class="work-head reveal">
        <span class="kicker kicker--accent">PROVE</span>
        <h1 class="work-title display">
          From ideas to measurable signal in one week.
        </h1>
        <p class="work-lede">
          PROVE is an operating model for rapidly validating product hypotheses through aggressively scoped one-week MVPs. It combines structured discovery, disciplined scope and rapid execution into a repeatable system that became Utsuk's default operating model.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="work-content">
    <div class="page">
      <div class="content-block reveal">
        <h2>The Problem</h2>
        <p>
          Most Proof of Concepts fail silently. They consume months, consume budgets, and produce unclear results. By the time the PoC ends, nobody remembers what hypothesis they were testing.
        </p>
        <p>
          The problem isn't that PoCs are ambitious. It's that they're <em>vaguely</em> ambitious. They try to prove too much. Build too much. Validate too much. And by doing everything, they validate nothing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block reveal">
        <h2>The Core Insight</h2>
        <p>
          Success isn't measured by features built. It's measured by uncertainty reduced.
        </p>
        <p>
          A successful PoC doesn't build a product. It answers one critical question with enough conviction that the team can move forward with confidence. Everything else is scope creep.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block reveal">
        <h2>The Framework</h2>
        <p>
          PROVE operates in five disciplined phases:
        </p>
        <div class="principle-list">
          <div class="principle-item">
            <h3>Problem Thesis (Day 1)</h3>
            <p>
              What hypothesis are we testing? What customer problem are we solving? What does success look like?
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle-item">
            <h3>Ruthless Scope (Day 1-2)</h3>
            <p>
              What is the <em>minimum</em> we need to build to test this hypothesis? What can we eliminate? What's the core interaction?
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle-item">
            <h3>Rapid Build (Day 2-5)</h3>
            <p>
              Build only what's in scope. Use templates, patterns, and existing components. Speed matters more than polish.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle-item">
            <h3>Structured Validation (Day 5-6)</h3>
            <p>
              Test the core hypothesis with real users. Use structured interviews, not casual conversations. Measure signals, not sentiment.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle-item">
            <h3>Clear Decision (Day 7)</h3>
            <p>
              Based on validation, go/no-go on the hypothesis. Build a case for what's next, not what failed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block reveal">
        <h2>Key Principles</h2>
        <ul class="content-list">
          <li><strong>Scope is sacred</strong> — Defending scope is more important than defending timeline. One week means one week.</li>
          <li><strong>Hypothesis-driven</strong> — Everything is in service of answering one question. Features that don't answer that question are out.</li>
          <li><strong>Signal over sentiment</strong> — We measure whether users can complete the core task, not whether they like it.</li>
          <li><strong>Document your decision</strong> — At the end, publish why you're moving forward (or not), not just whether you are.</li>
          <li><strong>One critical path</strong> — Don't build multiple features. Build one core interaction and test it thoroughly.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block reveal">
        <h2>Results</h2>
        <p>
          After implementing PROVE, engagement on new PoCs shifted dramatically:
        </p>
        <ul class="content-list">
          <li>Time to validation went from 3-4 months to 1 week</li>
          <li>Clear go/no-go decisions increased from 34% to 89%</li>
          <li>PoCs that moved to production increased from 12% to 43%</li>
          <li>Team alignment on success criteria jumped from 42% to 96%</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block reveal">
        <h2>The Multiplication Effect</h2>
        <p>
          By running structured one-week PoCs, teams can test multiple hypotheses in a month. The learning compounds. Subsequent PoCs benefit from earlier learnings. The organization moves faster not just through speed, but through accumulation of strategic knowledge.
        </p>
        <p>
          That's what made PROVE work as a system—it wasn't just about delivering one PoC faster. It was about making the entire organization faster at learning.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .work-hero {
    padding-block-start: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 3.5rem);
    padding-block-end: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 3.5rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .work-content {
    padding-block-start: clamp(2.5rem, 8vh, 4.5rem);
    padding-block-end: clamp(3rem, 10vh, 5rem);
  }

  .hero-content {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--w-page);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--gutter);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vh, 2rem);
  }

  .work-breadcrumb a {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    text-decoration: none;
    display: inline-block;
    transition: color 250ms;
  }
  .work-breadcrumb a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .work-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 3.2rem);
    max-width: 16ch;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .work-lede {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.4vh, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .page {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--w-page);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--gutter);
  }

  .content-block {
    margin-bottom: clamp(3rem, 8vh, 4.5rem);
  }

  .content-block h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .content-block p {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
  }

  .content-block p em {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .principle-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .principle-list {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .principle-item {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--paper-alt);
  }

  .principle-item h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .principle-item p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .content-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.8rem;
  }

  .content-list li {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .content-list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.65em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .content-list strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 650;
  }
</style>
